# Simple OS – base system
sudo
locales
network-manager
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
# iw: Wi-Fi state (link rate, power saving) for Report a Problem and troubleshooting
iw
libpam-systemd
# NTP time synchronization: systemd only Recommends it and the image is built without Recommends – without it the
# clock is never corrected (drifts; wrong by the time zone offset on a dual-boot with Windows)
systemd-timesyncd
polkitd
# pkexec: graphical password prompt (lxpolkit) for installations from the Setup Wizard
pkexec
# The tools every tutorial and install script assumes (curl/wget downloads, unzip/zip archives, ssh); the image is
# built without Recommends and Priority: standard, so none of them was there (~10 MB)
curl
wget
unzip
zip
openssh-client
# The first thing most guides ask for (git clone …); ~45 MB
git
dosfstools
exfatprogs
ntfs-3g
zram-tools
# Boot splash
plymouth
plymouth-themes
# Performance: gamemode (CPU/GPU boost for games). No preload: unmaintained since 2009, little use on SSDs, costs RAM
gamemode
